&lt;p&gt;We’re building a new Service Operations function within Customer Success to modernize how we structure, access, and act on customer data. This is a foundational role: you’ll be the primary consumer of the data built and owned by Business Systems, transforming it into automated reporting and AI-assisted tools that enable customer health tracking, streamline QBRs and EBRs, and provide executives with clear visibility into customer outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the reporting and automation layer for Customer Success&lt;/strong&gt; — translate stakeholder needs for account health, QBR/EBR decks, and executive dashboards into field-level requirements, then build the reporting and automation on top of the Customer Success data mart.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Default to AI-first workflows&lt;/strong&gt; — shape the roadmap for both deterministic (data plumbing) and non-deterministic (AI/LLM-driven) automation that surfaces customer insights, health checks, and recurring reports, replacing manual, ad hoc work wherever possible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automate recurring Customer Success workflows beyond reporting&lt;/strong&gt;, including renewal/adoption tracking, repetitive support tasks like ticket triage and diagnostics, and cross-platform automation that connects support tools (e.g., Zendesk) with systems like Salesforce, Slack, and the data warehouse to cut down manual handoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help define a secure, auditable data access model&lt;/strong&gt; for Customer Success workflows, in partnership with Business Systems and Security (who own implementation).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintain data quality and documentation&lt;/strong&gt; for Customer Success data sources, flagging gaps, inconsistencies, or governance issues as you find them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner across Business Systems, Product/Engineering, and Customer Success (TAM and Support)&lt;/strong&gt; to shape how data flows into the reports and tools people use every day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
