&lt;p&gt;The HRM is an owner/operator with range.&amp;nbsp; This role runs employee relations cases end to end, partners with managers on performance and coaching, own lifecycle programs from orientation through offboarding, and co-leads people programs like engagement and performance cycles. The right person is comfortable moving between tactical execution and advisory work on the same day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee Lifecycle&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own new hire Day One orientation and the onboarding experience across global time zones, partnering with Talent Acquisition, IT, and hiring managers; continuously improve content to reflect company strategy and culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage offboarding and terminations case by case: exit logistics, severance tracking, exit interviews, etc. Partner with IT and legal holds to ensure a smooth, compliant and complete transition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure lifecycle events (transfers, promotions, manager changes) are handled consistently and documented accurately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee Relations &amp;amp; Business Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary HR partner for a select client group: coach on performance conversations, team dynamics, and difficult situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own employee relations cases end to end (intake, investigation, documentation, resolution), escalating to the Sr. Director of HR and Legal as appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own leave management: coordinate leaves of absence (via Tilt), accommodations, and return-to-work plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted, approachable first point of contact for employee questions on policies, time off, and workplace concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Payroll (Domestic &amp;amp; Global)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own payroll execution by managing external Payroll Consultant across the US and international geos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance and the HR Operations Manager for accurate, timely processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Programs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-lead culture and engagement programs with the HR Operations Manager: All-Hands logistics, recognition, employer branding, and the engagement calendar/roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage engagement and benefits surveys; analyze trends and bring recommendations to the People team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support performance review cycles alongside the Sr. Director of HR, including manager enablement and communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommend and lead new initiatives to enhance culture and communication across the organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance &amp;amp; Operations Flex&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support accurate employee records in Rippling HRIS and support audits, documentation, and compliance reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support multi-state and global employment compliance in partnership with the HR Operations Manager and Legal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flex into HR operations projects (systems, workflows, vendor coordination) as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–8+ years of progressive HR experience, including time as an HR Generalist or HRBP in a high-growth tech or startup environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years demonstrated experience as a HR business partner to select client groups, preferably with technical teams (manager coaching, performance management, organizational guidance, etc)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience managing employee relations cases and leaves of absence with sound judgment, discretion, and clean documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of US multi-state employment practices and exposure to supporting employees internationally (UK, AU, CA, or via EOR).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payroll coordination and HRIS administration; Rippling experience strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program management experience: able to run engagement, survey, and performance-cycle programs end to end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ambiguity and context-switching on a lean team: equally effective owning a sensitive ER case and setting up a new hire&#39;s Day One.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to handle confidential information with integrity and build trust at every level of the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
